# Font Families: Sans, Serif & Mono 🔤

Tailwind provides three core font family utilities with modern, multi-tier system font fallbacks.

## Core Font Family Utilities

| Class | Font Stack | Best Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| `font-sans` | `ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, Apple Color Emoji...` | General app interfaces, buttons, titles |
| `font-serif` | `ui-serif, Georgia, Cambria, 'Times New Roman'...` | Editorial articles, books, classical design |
| `font-mono` | `ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas...` | Code snippets, terminal logs, tabular numbers |

## Customizing Fonts in Config

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      fontFamily: {
        inter: ['Inter', 'sans-serif'],
        code: ['Fira Code', 'monospace'],
      },
    },
  },
};
```

# Extending Colors in tailwind.config.js 🎨

Add your brand guidelines to Tailwind while keeping all default palette colors intact:

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        brand: {
          50: '#f0fdf4',
          100: '#dcfce7',
          500: '#22c55e',
          600: '#16a34a',
          900: '#14532d',
        },
        cyberpunk: '#f700ff',
      },
    },
  },
};
```

Use them immediately: `bg-brand-500`, `text-cyberpunk`, `border-brand-100`.
